00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But it was still love.

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:42.722 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was still love.

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:43.656 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Hey, so this is a show

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:46.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is based on children'
books, as I mentioned.

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:49.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you familiar with it
at all?

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.864 line:92%
-I wasn't familiar with it

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.434 line:92%
It was after my time as a kid.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:58.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I did read them
after I got the part.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:00.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughs ]
In the bathtub.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For those who aren't
familiar with it,

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:05.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
tell us a little bit
about the show.

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:09.182
-So, the show takes place
in a parallel universe.

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:12.452
And there's lots of cars
and they're crashing -- No

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:15.021 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:19.292
It's a parallel universe
of an alternate timeline.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:22.195 line:92%
But there's an evil source

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:25.698
that's sending subliminal
messages out into society.

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:30.036
And everybody is sort of anxious
about a big emergency

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:32.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they feel like
they're perpetually in.

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:37.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the only people
who can really suss it out

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.712 size:88% position:44%
and get to the bottom of
what this emergency is

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:44.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
and who is sending the signals
is a group of children,

00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:45.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is --
that is my favorite part

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:50.590
because children are innocent,
you know, when they're born.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:53.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then they turn into us
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:57.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so this story kind of like
highlights as a superpower

00:04:57.697 --> 00:05:01.601
the innocence that we all have
at the beginning of our lives.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:05.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You shot this show
in Vancouver.

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:08.474
-Yep.
-And I've heard that you came to

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:14.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
the observation that Canadians
maybe don't love sarcasm

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:16.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
as much as
their southern neighbors.

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:20.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I don't want to
start a war.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But yeah.

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:23.523 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I kind of found that.

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:25.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't mean
to blanket statements,

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:29.862
stereotype all Canadians
because I have some dear -

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:33.232
some of the -- you know,
Tim McAuliffe, Katie Crown

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:36.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
We can list
a slew of Canadians --

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:38.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jim Carrey, I don't know -
that are really funny.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:45.578
But in general, I found that
the average Canadian citizen

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:48.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
is not very familiar
with sarcasm.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:53.986
And to be fair, sarcasm is jus
a negative, nasty form of humor,

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:57.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Canadians are polite,
sweet people.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:00.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah. I would be like --
For instance,

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
we had to drive to a locatio
at a box store.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was getting
further and further away,

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:08.801 size:78% position:39%
even though there was
identical box stores.

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:10.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
We finally got to
our destination.

00:06:10.737 --> 00:06:13.106
And I looked at the driver
I was like, "I don't know.

00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:14.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm wondering
if you could drive me

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little further to
the next box store," you know?

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he just stopped
and he looked at me.

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:21.981
And he was like, "I'm sorry,
I don't know what you mean."

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:24.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, he was just like,
"What is it?"

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:25.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like,
"Of course you don't

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:27.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's just
a stupid, nasty joke."

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:30.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughs ]
So, yeah.

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:31.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're not really --
I promise you,

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:34.927
you're going to get into trouble
if you use sarcasm in Canada

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:37.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just be careful.
-Well, that's a very nice

00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:39.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
public service announcemen
for everybody watching.

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:42.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations on the show.
-If you can get there.

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:45.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Borders are closed, pal.

00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:48.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
No one's going.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:49.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:06:49.976 --> 00:06:52.011 size:88% position:44%
And I do hope next time
I can see you in person.

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:55.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I would like to look at
your face when I'm talking

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:58.751 line:92%
I've been staring at this stamp.

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:00.486 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So I could look at you.

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:01.621 line:92%
And I know you're handsome

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:04.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm just looking
at America now.

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:08.194
-Next time I'll send you a
Seth Meyers commemorative stamp.

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:10.129 line:92%
It'll make it a little easier.

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:10.897 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-But you'll get one.

00:07:10.897 --> 00:07:14.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks for having me on
the last night of Conan's show

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:16.803 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

